<title>INDIA: HOCKEY-INDIAN CAPTAIN PARGAT SINGH RETIRES.</title>
<headline>HOCKEY-INDIAN CAPTAIN PARGAT SINGH RETIRES.</headline>
<dateline>NEW DELHI 1997-01-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Hockey captain Pargat Singh, 32, the only player to lead India in two Olympics, in Barcelona and Atlanta, announced his retirement on Wednesday.</p>
<p>&quot;Its time to give the reins to younger players,&quot; said Singh, who was capped for a record 313 matches, captaining India 168 times.</p>
